WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:04.860
Tons of beloved Nintendo characters make&nbsp;
their big-screen debut in "The Super Mario&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:10.380
Bros. Movie," but viewers have noticed two missing&nbsp;
fan favorites who consider themselves number one.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:13.740
Warning: Spoilers for "The&nbsp;
Super Mario Bros. Movie" ahead.

00:00:13.740 --> 00:00:18.900
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie" gets a ton of&nbsp;
mileage out of video game lore, and there are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.880
Easter eggs pretty much everywhere you look. For&nbsp;
example, a Toad blows into a video game cartridge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:28.573
like how people would do with the NES or&nbsp;
N64 when it wouldn't work for some reason.

00:00:28.573 --> 00:00:30.892
"This thing work?"

00:00:30.892 --> 00:00:33.694
"Yes, you just have to blow into it."

00:00:33.694 --> 00:00:36.000
However, at a brisk 90-minute runtime,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.480
there are some bits of Mario mythology&nbsp;
that didn't make it into the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:44.220
and perhaps nothing is as disappointing&nbsp;
as the exclusion of Wario and Waluigi.

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:48.120
Granted, many other characters in the orbit&nbsp;
of Mario have yet to make their big-screen&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:53.520
animated debut, such as Daisy and Bowser&nbsp;
Jr. But Wario and Waluigi have a unique,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.780
idiosyncratic appeal to them, and people were&nbsp;
no doubt wondering when they were going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.700
show up. That's especially true since Mario&nbsp;
and Luigi have an antagonistic relationship&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:08.640
with their former co-worker, Spike. He could've&nbsp;
easily been Wario, and Mario fans, along with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:13.320
people who love the Wario and Waluigi memes all&nbsp;
over social media, would've lost their minds.

00:01:13.320 --> 00:01:16.620
But, of course, the two archrivals&nbsp;
of the Mario Brothers could still&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.620 --> 00:01:20.400
get their moment. There are naturally&nbsp;
many places the franchise can go as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:24.180
far as sequels. The post-credits scene&nbsp;
hints that Yoshi will be involved in some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.180 --> 00:01:28.800
capacity next time around. Bowser is still&nbsp;
around, though tiny and locked in a cage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.600
But a sequel should explore other antagonists&nbsp;
and other facets of this realm, and there would&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:47.062
"The Super Mario Bros. Movie," Mario and Luigi got&nbsp;
picked on in their youth. The movies could reveal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:51.142
that Wario was one of those bullies, though&nbsp;
other stories have usually portrayed him as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.934 --> 00:02:03.534
They could even be the ones responsible&nbsp;
for letting Bowser out of his imprisonment,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:07.554
leading to a team-up while potentially&nbsp;
exploring other lands or galaxies.

00:02:07.554 --> 00:02:11.994
Making it so that Wario and Waluigi come&nbsp;
from Brooklyn would also be an intriguing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.994 --> 00:02:16.674
development by forcing Mario and Luigi to&nbsp;
confront their roots. By the end of "The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.674 --> 00:02:20.214
Super Mario Bros. Movie," the brothers&nbsp;
are living in the Mushroom Kingdom after&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.214 --> 00:02:24.774
finally earning the approval of their father.&nbsp;
They appear to have finally found contentment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.774 --> 00:02:27.954
in their lives, but their past could&nbsp;
come back to haunt them in a big way.

00:02:27.954 --> 00:02:31.314
With decades of games, there's no&nbsp;
shortage of stories to pull from&nbsp;&nbsp;

